.\" QtDMM manual page. CMake fills in version and date (docs/qtdmm.1.in).
.\" The options must match src/main.cpp - tests/generate_docs.py --check
.\" (ctest docs_generated) compares them.
.TH QTDMM 1 "@QTDMM_MAN_DATE@" "QtDMM @QTDMM_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qtdmm \- read out and record digital multimeters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qtdmm
.RB [ \-\-config\-id
.IR id ]
.RB [ \-\-config\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-connect
.IR id ]...
.RB [ \-\-vxi11\-rpc
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-\-vxi11\-portmapper\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.RB [ \-\-debug\-device
.IR id ]
.br
.B qtdmm
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help " | " \-v " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B QtDMM
reads digital multimeters and bench meters and shows the reading as an LCD
display and an analog meter. A configurable recorder draws the readings as a
graph. It can start by hand, at a set time or when a threshold is crossed, and
exports to CSV, Excel (.xlsx), OpenDocument (.ods), SVG, PDF, PNG and JPEG.
.PP
More than 150 meters are supported, connected over:
.IP \(bu 2
serial ports and USB\-serial cables;
.IP \(bu 2
USB\-HID cables such as the UNI\-T UT\-D04/UT\-D09 and Brymen BU\-86X;
.IP \(bu 2
the network (RFC 2217, for example through
.BR qtdmm\-bridge );
.IP \(bu 2
Bluetooth LE (UNI\-T UT60BT, Victron battery monitors, solar chargers and
inverters);
.IP \(bu 2
.BR sigrok\-cli (1)
for SCPI bench meters.
.PP
Further features are a readings table, alarms with actions, calculated values
across several meters, a simulated meter for trying QtDMM without hardware, and
an SCPI server through which other programs read the meter over the network.
The complete handbook is built into the program (Help) and online at
.UR https://qtdmm.de/docs/
.UE .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-id " id"
Use the configuration
.I id
instead of
.BR default .
Each id has its own settings file: its window, its views and the devices it
connects; QtDMMs with different ids run side by side, without a link.
An id of letters, digits and underscores (not starting with a digit) can be
used in the formula of a calculated value.
.TP
.BI \-\-connect " id"
Connect the entry
.I id
of My devices at the start, after the devices connected last time; repeat the
option for more. Its readings reach the SCPI server
.RB ( INSTrument:SELect ),
and it records with the other devices;
.B QTDMM:DEVice:CATalog?
lists the ids.
.TP
.BI \-\-also " id"
The same as
.B \-\-connect
(its name before 26.4).
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-dir " dir"
Keep the configuration files in
.I dir
instead of the platform's user configuration directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-vxi11\-rpc " mode"
Where the VXI\-11 server of the SCPI server gets its portmapper from, for this
run only:
.B auto
(the system's
.BR rpcbind (8)
when it runs, otherwise an own one),
.B system
or
.B own
(port 111 itself, which needs the right to bind a privileged port).
Replaces the setting without changing it.
.TP
.BI \-\-vxi11\-portmapper\-port " port"
For tests and development: the VXI\-11 server with an own portmapper on
.I port
instead of 111
.RB ( 0 :
any free one), for this run only; implies
.BR "\-\-vxi11\-rpc own" .
VISA libraries and lxi\-tools ask port 111 and do not find it there.
.TP
.BI \-\-debug\-device " id"
Print only the frames of the entry
.I id
of My devices; repeat it for more.
Without the HID, Bluetooth and service messages of
.BR \-\-debug .
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print every frame received from the meter as a line of hex bytes on
standard output.
Include this output, together with what the meter displayed, in a bug report
about a meter that is not decoded correctly.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/QtDMM/QtDMM.conf
Settings of the
.B default
configuration (Linux, FreeBSD and macOS).
.TP
.IR ~/.config/QtDMM/QtDMM_ id .conf
Settings of the configuration
.IR id .
.TP
.I %APPDATA%\eQtDMM\eQtDMM.ini
Settings on Windows; further ids as
.IR QtDMM_ id .ini .
.TP
.I ~/.config/QtDMM/devices.conf
My devices: the meters with their connections, shared by all instances
(on Windows
.IR %APPDATA%\eQtDMM\edevices.conf ).
.SH EXAMPLES
Start a second instance for another meter:
.PP
.RS
.B qtdmm \-\-config\-id psu
.RE
.PP
Capture the raw frames of a meter for a bug report:
.PP
.RS
.B qtdmm \-\-debug > frames.txt
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sigrok\-cli (1)
.PP
Handbook:
.UR https://qtdmm.de/docs/
.UE
.br
Source and bug reports:
.UR https://github.com/qtdmm/QtDMM
.UE
.br
Contact: hello@qtdmm.de
